  "details": "I load into VR chat on desktop or VR wise, and some avatars are robots in order for me to load them. I keep turning on and off their avatars for it to actually fall load in, but then sometimes when I have no avatar shown and I go to a public world, for example a Apodo‘s world that is a sonic theme world in VR chat I get five to eight frames per second. I also don’t have to preload worlds in order to actually go in them and it’s just kind of not working. And when someone does stickers or emojis or sometimes print, it says no image found. When I also tried putting on the new accessories or show my items they go invisible sometimes. I know one of my friends has the same issues, but I don’t know if she has tried reaching out to support. But then when I switch over to coyest side, cause I request VR headset, I don’t see emojis or stickers, one place it doesn’t say no image found or anything. It’s just not there, but I hear it being placed down for the stickers.. then I’m getting a message saying my VR headset doesn’t have enough memory, but it wasn’t doing that before and I also factory reset my headset to fix it and it did not.",
